    "Business Need: Managed Database",
    "Emma is concerned about:",
    "• Business data tracked in a spreadsheet on a",
    "local PC, which must be with her at all times.",
    "• Potential to lose financial, point of sale (POS),",
    "and labor data.",
    "• Spreadsheet is not secured, and is becoming",
    "challenging to use.",
    "• No way to know when ingredient supplies are",
    "getting low.",
    "• If the EC2 instance that hosts the order history",
    "database fails, they will lose all their data."
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "img": "img/p-50.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P051",
   "texts": [
    "Sophie’s Database Request",
    "Sophie calls Alejandro about creating a database. She",
    "suggests a solution that aligns with AWS Best Practices",
    "within the Well Architected Framework.",
    "However, Alejandro points out larger concerns:",
    "• All the café’s order data is on one EC2 instance",
    "• This creates a potential for failure, which could shut them",
    "down",
    "Alejandro suggests the order history should be migrated to",
    "Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS).",
    "Supply chain contact information should also be imported",
    "from the Emma’s laptop to Amazon RDS."
   ],
